            <ArticleTitle>A descriptive case series: oral transmucosal fentanyl use in patients with noncancerous pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>81-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Transmucosal fentanyl is indicated for patients with cancer who are opioid tolerant, but it is also used for the treatment of noncancerous pain. The following is a survey study of the use of transmucosal fentanyl in 29 patients with noncancerous pain in an academic, community-based pain management practice. Transmucosal fentanyl was found to be safe and efficacious in the patients studied.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
